# EduRankAI — environment reference
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy to `.env.local` (dev) and fill in. NEVER commit a filled copy: `.env*` is
# gitignored and `.env.production` on the founder's machine holds live credentials.
#
# HOW TO READ THIS FILE
#   [live]   read by code in src/ today. Removing it changes behaviour now.
#   [stack]  read by the Docker mail stack (docker/compose*.yml), not by the Astro app.
#   [future] reserved by the mail-platform design; nothing reads it yet. Listed so the
#            name is fixed once and every patch uses the same spelling.
#
# Names are the ones the code ACTUALLY reads (verified with a grep over src/ and
# scripts/). Where the Patch-4 brief used a different spelling, the deviation is
# noted inline — the brief is not authoritative over shipped code, and silently
# renaming a variable the app reads is an outage.
#
# Validate a real environment against this file:  node scripts/mail-env-check.mjs

# ===========================================================================
# 1. DATABASE  (Supabase Postgres, transaction pooler)
# ===========================================================================
# [live] The only connection string the app uses. Port 6543 is the Supabase
# transaction pooler; 5432 is the direct/session connection. Serverless MUST use
# 6543 — the direct port runs out of connections under Vercel's concurrency.
# Transaction pooling does not support prepared statements: keep `prepare: false`
# in src/lib/db.ts if you ever change this.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.PROJECTREF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# [future] Direct (session-mode) URL. pg_dump, drizzle-kit and anything needing
# prepared statements or advisory locks want this, NOT the pooler.
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT=postgresql://postgres.PROJECTREF:PASSWORD@aws-0-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres

# [future] Supabase REST/storage/auth surface. The app talks to Postgres directly
# today and uses none of these; they are listed because the mail platform's storage
# adapter (docs/mail/MIGRATION.md section 3) may use Supabase Storage before S3.
SUPABASE_URL=https://PROJECTREF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SECRET. Bypasses row-level security. Server-side only — never in a client bundle,
# never in a Vercel variable exposed to the browser, never in a log line.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ===========================================================================
# 2. MAIL — identity and domain
# ===========================================================================
# [live] src/lib/mail.ts:15. The domain internal mailboxes are addressed under.
MAIL_DOMAIN=edurankai.in
# [live] src/lib/email.ts:18, last-resort From when mail_config has no row.
EMAIL_FROM=EduRankAI <noreply@edurankai.in>
# [stack] Hostname the MTA announces in HELO/EHLO and in Received: headers.
# Must have forward+reverse DNS that agree, or large receivers will refuse you.
MAIL_HOST=mail.edurankai.in
# [stack] Submission port the local stack listens on for authenticated clients.
MAIL_PORT=587

# ===========================================================================
# 3. MAIL — outbound SMTP
# ===========================================================================
# NOTE ON NAMES: the brief said SMTP_USERNAME / SMTP_PASSWORD. The code reads
# SMTP_USER / SMTP_PASS (src/lib/mail.ts getMailConfig). The code wins.
# Also: in production these values normally come from the `mail_config` DB row
# edited at /admin/mail/settings, which OVERRIDES env. Env is the fallback.
SMTP_HOST=smtpout.secureserver.net
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=connect@edurankai.in
SMTP_PASS=
# [live] true only for port 465 (implicit TLS). Port 587 is STARTTLS -> false.
SMTP_SECURE=false
# [live] Accept a self-signed server certificate. Leave false. Setting this true
# on a public relay silently disables MITM protection for every message you send.
SMTP_INSECURE=false

# ===========================================================================
# 4. MAIL — inbound
# ===========================================================================
# [live] src/pages/api/mail/inbound.ts. Shared secret an MTA/worker presents in
# `x-mail-secret`. The DB value (mail_config.inbound_secret) wins over this.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
MAIL_INBOUND_SECRET=
# [future] HMAC key for signed inbound webhooks (src/lib/mailops/webhook.ts).
# Preferred over the bare shared secret: the signature covers the body and a
# timestamp, so a captured request cannot be replayed. openssl rand -hex 32
MAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# [future] Replay window in seconds for signed webhooks. Below 30 you will reject
# honest requests on clock skew; above 600 a captured request stays useful too long.
MAIL_WEBHOOK_TOLERANCE_SECONDS=300

# ===========================================================================
# 5. SERVICE-TO-SERVICE (Vercel API  ->  ZBook mail service)
# ===========================================================================
# The browser NEVER talks to the mail service. Browser -> Vercel API -> mail service.
# [future] Base URL of the mail service as seen FROM Vercel. Public hostname +
# TLS, or a tunnel. Never a private RFC1918 address — Vercel cannot route to it.
MAIL_SERVICE_URL=https://mail.edurankai.in
# [future] HMAC key shared by the Vercel app and the mail service. Distinct from
# MAIL_WEBHOOK_SECRET so a leak of one direction does not compromise the other.
MAIL_SERVICE_KEY=
# [future] Comma-separated origins allowed to call the browser-facing mail API.
# Never `*` for a credentialed endpoint. src/lib/mailops/cors.ts.
MAIL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://www.edurankai.in,https://edurankai.in

# ===========================================================================
# 6. REDIS / QUEUE
# ===========================================================================
# The job queue in production is POSTGRES (`edu_jobs`, src/lib/job-queue.ts) and
# needs no Redis. Redis is the local-stack and future-scale option; it is not a
# dependency of the shipped app. Do not let its presence here imply otherwise.
# [stack] Local compose value: redis://redis:6379
REDIS_URL=
# [future] Which queue driver the mail worker uses: postgres | redis
QUEUE_DRIVER=postgres
# [future] Jobs claimed per worker tick. src/lib/job-queue.ts claimBatch() default 20.
QUEUE_BATCH_SIZE=20
# [future] Attempts before a job is parked as failed. Backoff 1s,2s,4s… capped 5m.
QUEUE_MAX_ATTEMPTS=5
# [future] Worker poll interval, milliseconds.
QUEUE_POLL_INTERVAL_MS=2000
# [future] Concurrent outbound SMTP deliveries per worker. Raising this without
# raising the MTA's own concurrency just moves the queue, it does not drain it.
QUEUE_CONCURRENCY=4

# ===========================================================================
# 7. STORAGE  (attachments, message bodies at scale)
# ===========================================================================
# [live] Vercel Blob. Works today; NOT the long-term target — the sovereignty rule
# is S3-compatible storage you can host. docs/mail/MIGRATION.md section 3.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
# [live, all five required] S3-compatible storage. The storage layer picks S3 over
# Blob only when EVERY one of these is set. Four out of five = silently still Blob.
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_REGION=
S3_BUCKET=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# [live] Public read base for objects, if the bucket is fronted by a CDN.
S3_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
# [future] Attachment ceiling accepted by the mail API, bytes. 25 MB is what most
# receivers accept after base64 expansion; above that, send a link.
MAIL_MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES=26214400

# ===========================================================================
# 8. DKIM
# ===========================================================================
# The private key is the single most sensitive file in the mail stack: with it,
# anyone can sign mail as you. It is NOT in the repository and NOT in this file —
# these variables point at it. Backup policy: docs/mail/BACKUP.md section 2.
# [stack] Selector published as <selector>._domainkey.<domain> TXT.
DKIM_SELECTOR=era1
# [stack] Domain the key signs for.
DKIM_DOMAIN=edurankai.in
# [stack] Path to the private key INSIDE the container (mounted, mode 0600).
DKIM_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/etc/dkim/era1.private
# [future] Alternative to the path: the PEM itself, for platforms with no file
# mount (Vercel). Newlines as \n. Prefer the path when a mount exists.
DKIM_PRIVATE_KEY=

# ===========================================================================
# 9. SESSIONS / JWT
# ===========================================================================
# [live] Session cookies are OPAQUE TOKENS in Postgres (src/lib/auth/session.ts),
# not JWTs. The brief asked for "JWT configuration"; this system does not issue
# JWTs for user sessions and adding one would be a second auth path to keep in
# sync. The JWT vars below are for SERVICE tokens only (mail service <-> app).
SESSION_SECRET=
SESSION_COOKIE_NAME=era_session
# [future] Signing key for short-lived service JWTs. HS256. Rotate by issuing a
# new key and accepting both for one TTL.
MAIL_JWT_SECRET=
# [future] Service token lifetime, seconds. Keep it short — these are minted
# per-request, not held.
MAIL_JWT_TTL_SECONDS=300

# ===========================================================================
# 10. OBSERVABILITY
# ===========================================================================
# [live] Bearer token for GET /api/metrics. MUST BE AT LEAST 32 CHARACTERS — the endpoint
# treats a shorter or absent token as "this door does not exist" and answers 403, so a
# 20-character token fails in a way that looks like a wrong token rather than a short one.
# An operator session with the platform `administer` capability is the other way in.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
METRICS_TOKEN=
# [stack] Grafana initial admin password. Change on first login.
GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# [live] Set by Vercel. Used by deployMarker() to stamp which commit is serving.
VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA=
VERCEL_ENV=

# ===========================================================================
# 11. CRON / WEBHOOKS (existing, listed for completeness)
# ===========================================================================
# [live] Guards /api/*/cron routes. WHITESPACE IN THIS VALUE REJECTS EVERY VERCEL
# DEPLOY in about 2 seconds, with an error that does not name the variable.
CRON_SECRET=
# [live] Razorpay webhook signature key. src/pages/api/payments/*.
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# [live] Proctoring vendor callback signature key. Advisory-only pipeline.
PROCTORING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ===========================================================================
# 12. LOCAL STACK TOGGLES  (docker/compose*.yml only)
# ===========================================================================
# [stack] Where the local app gets its database:
#   supabase  — use DATABASE_URL above (DEFAULT; keeps one source of truth)
#   local     — use the postgres container from docker/compose.db.yml (profile: localdb)
LOCAL_DB_MODE=supabase
# [stack] Local Postgres, only when LOCAL_DB_MODE=local.
POSTGRES_USER=era
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=era_local_dev_only
POSTGRES_DB=era
# [stack] Where the local stack sends outbound mail during tests.
#   sink   — scripts/smtp-sink.mjs, captures to disk, delivers NOTHING (DEFAULT)
#   local  — the Postfix container, which will attempt real delivery
# Never set this to `local` on a machine that can reach the public internet
# unless you intend to actually send. docs/mail/TESTING.md section 4.
LOCAL_SMTP_MODE=sink
# [stack] Host ports. Changed here rather than in the compose file so a second
# checkout can run alongside the first.
PORT_APP=4321
PORT_SMTP=1025
PORT_SUBMISSION=1587
PORT_IMAP=1143
PORT_REDIS=6379
PORT_MAILOPS=9100
PORT_PROMETHEUS=9090
PORT_GRAFANA=3001
